   "daf": "44a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ אַרְבָּעָה אַחִין סָלְקָא דַּעְתָּךְ? אֶלָּא אֵימָא: אַרְבָּעָה מֵאַחִין.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The simple reading of the mishna’s first clause implies that all four brothers died. The Gemara questions this: Can it «enter your mind» to say that all «four brothers» died? If they all died, then who remains to consummate the levirate marriage? «Rather,» emend the mishna and «say» instead: «Four» married men «of» a set of more than four «brothers» died."
  }
